.DS_Store

# Bram local state — per-machine, never shared
.bram.json
.claude/
CLAUDE.md

# CLAUDE.md is tracked deliberately: it carries the project-authored
# Planner/Coder convention below Bram's marker block. The bram:start block
# itself is only a 3-line import, so it does not churn the way AGENTS.md did.
!CLAUDE.md
resources/

# Bram Setup rewrites AGENTS.md's <!-- bram:start --> block on every upgrade.
# In THIS repo the file is nothing but that block — zero lines outside the
# markers — so there is no human-authored contract to preserve and tracking it
# would commit pure machine scaffolding that goes dirty again on the next
# upgrade. Ignoring it is what actually gives this repo a clean `git status`.
#
# This differs from ludwa6/vdl-web on purpose. There, AGENTS.md IS tracked,
# because it carries Walt's own Planner/Coder contract; only the bram block is
# reverted by hand (standing instruction in that repo's issue #8). If a
# Planner/Coder contract is ever written for this repo, delete this line and
# adopt the vdl-web rule instead: track the file, exclude the block.
#
# Second reason, specific to this repo: it is public and its readers are the
# organisation's secretaries. A root-level file of agent worklist-gate
# instructions is noise for that audience.
AGENTS.md
